&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Account Executive for Singapore, you will own and grow GitLab’s enterprise relationships in the Singapore market. You’ll help large organizations realize the full value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform by leading the entire sales cycle, from prospecting and qualification through rollout and long-term adoption. Reporting to an Area Sales Manager or Regional Director, you’ll use a consultative approach to understand complex customer needs, guide them through evaluation, and coordinate pre- and post-sales resources to ensure successful deployments and visible business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work under minimal supervision on complex deals, act as the voice of the customer into GitLab, and partner closely with our strategic channel partners to generate qualified opportunities and develop new customers. In your first year, you’ll be expected to establish and execute clear account plans for enterprise prospects and customers in the Singapore market, build strong internal and external stakeholder relationships, and consistently manage your forecast and pipeline with transparency and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support GitLab’s strategic prospects and customers in the Singapore Market, with a focus in the financial services industry, owning the full sales cycle for large and enterprise accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead account strategy by developing and executing account plans aligned to each customer’s business needs and long-term goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct prospecting and opportunity development activities in named large and strategic accounts, including working closely with strategic channel partners to generate qualified leads and new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate pre- and post-sales engagement with solutions architects, customer success, and support teams to ensure successful rollout, adoption, and expansion of GitLab products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear account leadership, including regular activity, pipeline, and forecast reporting to sales management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze wins and losses, contribute to root cause analysis, and share lessons learned with account managers, marketing, and technical teams to improve future outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer by sharing feedback and product ideas through GitLab’s public issue tracker and internal channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a consultative sales approach to uncover business issues, shape solution recommendations, and deliver compelling proposals, quotes, and presentations that address customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles with large, strategic enterprise customers, ideally selling into Financial Services institutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to prospect, qualify, and develop new opportunities while also growing existing accounts through strong account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in leading pre- and post-sales activities, coordinating with technical, support, and channel partners to drive adoption and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in consultative selling, including uncovering business needs, building account plans, and delivering proposals and presentations that align GitLab solutions to customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prepare and maintain accurate activity, pipeline, and forecast reports, and to contribute to win/loss and root cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and collaboration skills to share customer feedback and lessons learned with sales management, product, marketing, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development concepts and tools, with preferred exposure to Git, software development tools, or application lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with GitLab’s values, openness to learning, and interest in applying transferable skills even if your background does not match every requirement exactly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Account Executive will join our enterprise sales team, which focuses on driving GitLab adoption with large customers in the Singapore market. The team is responsible for the full relationship lifecycle with enterprise accounts, from initial engagement through long-term expansion and advocacy, ensuring customers realize value from GitLab’s DevSecOps platform. Team members work in an all-remote, distributed environment and collaborate asynchronously across time zones with sales leadership, solutions architects, customer success, marketing, and channel partners. The team is currently focused on maintaining and growing our existing footprint in the region, executing a consistent global sales motion while adapting to local customer needs and partnering closely with strategic channel organizations to reach and support key accounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
