&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood is seeking a Senior Applications Engineer to join&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Build&lt;/strong&gt;, the small, high-leverage team that turns the company&#39;s best AI-built prototypes into true enterprise-grade services.&amp;nbsp;Robinhood&#39;s corporate ecosystem is deep, Okta identity, Google Workspace, Slack, ServiceNow, Atlassian, Salesforce, and the agent fabric that makes all of it agent-accessible. When a prototype graduates into a real service, someone has to make it a native citizen of that ecosystem: single sign-on and access done right, provisioning and audit wired in, data flowing to and from the systems of record, surfaces appearing where people already work. That someone is you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the front of the pipeline: when prototypes arrive at the team&#39;s intake, you perform the rapid technical assessment, what data it touches, what systems it needs, what would break, that determines whether it self-serves in the sandbox, becomes a Build engagement, or is better bought than built. You’ll partner with the team&#39;s SWEs, who rebuild prototypes from the ground up into production services. You determine how everything connects, with breadth across enterprise surfaces, and you personally deliver the many ‘graduations’ that are 80% integration, configuration, and workflow automation with 20% glue code, where a ground-up rebuild isn’t needed. Between builds, your intake assessments shape what the whole team does next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood operates in a heavily regulated industry: ambiguity is constant, playbooks are yours to write, and safe-by-default is the house style.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own intake assessment for the graduation pipeline: rapidly evaluate incoming prototypes, data classification, system touchpoints, integration surface, risk flags, and recommend the disposition: sandbox, build, or buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make graduated services native to the enterprise: SSO and access via Okta, SCIM provisioning, audit logging, and surfaces in Slack, Workspace, and ServiceNow where users already live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver integration-led graduations end-to-end where configuration, workflow automation, and targeted glue code beat a ground-up rebuild.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the MCP integrations and automations that connect Build&#39;s services to Robinhood&#39;s SaaS estate, and make them agent-accessible by default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with business partners to map their real workflow before anything is built, and stay their translator throughout the engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Enterprise Platforms on the identity and application-onboarding paved road, and with Enterprise Operations on clean operational handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply approved AI tools relentlessly to your own work: automate the repetitive parts of assessment, integration, and documentation so your time goes to judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience across a modern enterprise SaaS estate, Okta (identity, SSO, lifecycle), Google Workspace, Slack, ServiceNow, Atlassian, and with integration or workflow-automation platforms (e.g., Workato or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scripting and API fluency: Python or similar for glue code and automation, plus working depth in REST, webhooks, OAuth, and SCIM. You ship working integrations; you don&#39;t need to be a full-stack systems engineer, that&#39;s what your SWE teammates are for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of at least one significant service or platform area as its domain expert, with sound decisions under medium-to-high ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An assessor&#39;s eye: you can look at an unfamiliar app and quickly see what data it touches, what it depends on, and what it would take to run it safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical and communication skills, you translate technical complexity into clear guidance for both executives and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently in high-ambiguity situations, define scope where there is none, and build trust across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in highly regulated industries, particularly finance or fintech, is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
