&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain compensation models. You&#39;ll develop scalable models that support market benchmarking, budget planning, scenario analysis, and data reconciliation, delivering data-driven insights that inform compensation strategy and business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead compensation analytics. You&#39;ll drive survey participation, job matching, market pricing, and trend analyses to evaluate pay competitiveness and inform salary structures, equity bands, and compensation recommendations across global markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain reporting and trackers. You&#39;ll create and maintain compensation trackers, dashboards, and budgets, delivering accurate, timely reporting that stakeholders can rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer broad-based compensation. You&#39;ll support annual merit, promotion, and variable/incentive compensation cycles end to end, including planning, modeling, award generation, payroll/equity reconciliation, and post-cycle analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve compensation systems. You&#39;ll maintain and enhance the compensation tooling, job catalog, and databases used by the People and Recruiting teams, and design automations that reduce manual work and error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support M&amp;amp;A integration. You&#39;ll provide compensation analysis and support for mergers and acquisitions, including due diligence, harmonizing pay structures, and integrating acquired employees into Robinhood&#39;s programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Further AI and automation across the function. You&#39;ll use AI and modern tooling to enhance and streamline benchmarking, analysis, communications, and reporting, making processes faster and more accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally. You&#39;ll work with People Partners, HRIS, Finance, and Legal on year-round initiatives and ad-hoc analyses, ensuring clean data flows and clear communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
