&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Department&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Office of the CTO is the strategic engine for Cloudflare’s technology vision. We look beyond the horizon to identify emerging trends, drive technical innovation, and ensure our engineering culture remains principled and curious. We operate at the intersection of deep technical strategy and high-level business execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the CTO Operations Lead you will act as a strategic force multiplier for the Chief Technology Officer. Working alongside the CTO Chief of Staff you will help manage priorities, ensuring the CTO’s time is aligned with Cloudflare’s most critical technical and business goals. This role requires a blend of operational rigor, strategic thinking, and the ability to navigate complex cross-functional landscapes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate the rhythm of the business for the CTO department. This includes ensuring the department remains compliant with all training and regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Briefing &amp;amp; Preparation:&lt;/strong&gt; Research and synthesize context for the CTO ahead of external engagements and key customer calls. You will ensure the CTO is equipped with actionable insights, background data, and strategic talking points to maximize the impact of every interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Actionable Follow-Through:&lt;/strong&gt; Attend high-priority internal and external calls to capture critical context. You will own the lifecycle of action items, driving accountability across teams and ensuring that decisions made in meetings translate into tangible results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Narrative Construction:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the CTO to craft compelling presentations and written materials for internal all-hands, board meetings, and external keynotes. You will help translate complex technical concepts into clear, impactful narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead special projects and initiatives within the Office of the CTO, often navigating ambiguity to define scope, stakeholders, and success metrics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Examples of Desirable Skills, Knowledge and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Management Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated experience in technical program management, business operations, or a chief of staff-style role. You are comfortable managing complex timelines and multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. You can distill complex information into clear executive briefings and have experience creating high-quality presentation materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing operational data, including budgets, resource planning, or headcount allocation. You are comfortable using data to inform decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discretion &amp;amp; Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; High level of integrity and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential information. You possess the professional maturity to represent the Office of the CTO internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities can shift. You approach challenges with a solution-oriented mindset and are capable of working autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
