&lt;p&gt;As a Frontend Software Engineer on the Coinbase Card team within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer Product Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, you&#39;ll build and ship the user-facing experiences behind Coinbase&#39;s card products, including the Coinbase One Card (credit) and the Coinbase Card (debit). This team is consolidating both products onto a unified card platform, and you&#39;ll join a small team with high ownership, greenfield feature work, and direct impact on how millions of customers discover, activate, and use their cards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end frontend development for core card experiences, including transactions, rewards, onboarding, and account management across web and mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build new user-facing features - such as authorized card users, reward offers, real-time transaction status trackers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, and backend engineering to scope, prioritize, and ship projects that reduce CX contact rates and improve the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve frontend performance bottlenecks across card UX journeys, driving measurable improvements in CUJ latency and availability SLOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
