&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and product managers to define product requirements and translate them into clear, usable, and well-considered design solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct lightweight research and usability sessions with internal users to validate decisions and surface unmet needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a consistent design language across our internal tools suite, working in close coordination with the Sail Design team and the Stripe design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make design trade-offs confidently, knowing when to go deep on craft and when to ship a pragmatic solution that moves the product forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help raise the bar for internal product design at Stripe, advocating for users who are often underserved compared to customer-facing surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product design experience, with a portfolio that demonstrates strong UX thinking, clear visual craft, and an ability to navigate ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing tools for complex or data-heavy workflows—internal tools, developer tools, ops platforms, or similar are a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across the full design process—you can lead discovery, write a problem brief, design and prototype, and ship without needing every step handed to you&lt;/li&gt;
