&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a knowledgeable and proactive Technical Partner Manager to join our Global Partner Engineering &amp;amp; Operations (PE&amp;amp;O) Network partnerships team at Stripe. In this role, you will be responsible for building and maintaining strong relationships with our partners, facilitating technical integrations and launching new capabilities with new and existing partners, and ensuring the optimal performance of our solutions with financial partners. The ideal candidate will possess a blend of technical expertise and account management experience, with a focus on driving partner success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain strong, long-term relationships with key financial ecosystem partners, serving as the primary point of contact for technical inquiries and operational support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Integration: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate closely with partners to define and implement successful integrations, ensuring all technical requirements are met and projects are delivered on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Tracking: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish Service Level Agreements (SLAs) and performance standards for partner accounts, leveraging metrics and data analysis to monitor and improve partner health and satisfaction. Regularly drive technical reviews to improve partner performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work across multiple Stripe teams—including Engineering, Product, and Partner Development—to support and drive process enhancements and technical solutions that benefit partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Assist in incident resolution by coordinating with internal teams to manage partner communications effectively and resolve issues efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Computer Science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 6 years of experience in partner management, technical project management, or business operations, especially managing external partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment technologies and ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive medium to large-sized technical projects in collaboration with external partners and cross-functional internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, capable of effectively conveying technical information to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as necessary to meet partner needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic to intermediate proficiency in SQL and XML is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Technical Program Management team to build the systems that make global, programmable money trustworthy at scale. At Bridge, we’re not just improving global payments—we’re reinventing how money moves across borders using stablecoins and modern financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is about driving execution across complex technical initiatives—bringing structure to ambiguous problems, aligning stakeholders, and helping the team move quickly while maintaining reliability, performance, and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a TPM, you&#39;ll play a key role leading complex programs across multiple engineering, product, and cross-functional (finance, legal, compliance, risk, and other) teams spanning Bridge. You&#39;ll be an active contributor to the overall strategy of the program, drive technical decision-making, and drive the execution of the program through all phases from planning to delivery. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to implement mechanisms that make your programs effective and scale them to Bridge-level processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive functional and technical delivery of key team and org-wide programs and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering teams to design, scope, and shepherd features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create functional specs, project and release plans, and roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute one or more software engineering programs simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product decisions that align with program and company objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence senior stakeholders and build consensus across engineering, product, and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and scale program processes and frameworks that can be adopted across the org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor TPMs and contribute to building the TPM discipline at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in technical program or product management, with a consistent track record of shipping products with broad and global customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of providing solid program management during all phases of software development from kick-off to ship, demonstrating critical thinking and thought leadership throughout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re not satisfied with just delivering programs on time—you&#39;re discerning about product and infrastructure architecture and can lead technical discussions. You don’t let problems remain ambiguous and directly drive clarity on decision tradeoffs and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You operate independently and lead efforts across multiple teams and functions, with stakeholders in different disciplines across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong written and verbal communication skills to build relationships and collaborate with diverse cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience at a fintech or payments company. Track record of driving programs with cross-organizational or company-wide impact — not just team-level delivery. Comfortable working directly with senior engineering and product leadership with limited support. History of building toward durable, long-term solutions, not just shipping on time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Growth organization drives Stripe&#39;s self-serve growth engine: from a user&#39;s first interaction with Stripe through onboarding, activation, and expansion across our products. Growth focuses on building the systems and surfaces that help any user find, understand, and adopt the right set of Stripe products, regardless of how or where they start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Growth, the onboarding program is how new and existing users get to their first successful use of Stripe as quickly and completely as possible. A cohesive onboarding experience is critical to Stripe&#39;s ability to convert prospects, activate new products, and compete against increasingly sophisticated alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onboarding spans several interconnected surfaces:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquisition and intent capture — first-touch experiences that match prospects to the right products and entry points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account setup and activation — guided flows that get users live with the right integration shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-product discovery — contextual surfaces that help new and existing users adopt additional products over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These surfaces are deeply interdependent, span dozens of cross-functional teams, and directly shape Stripe&#39;s new user activation and product attach rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are seeking a product-focused Technical Program Manager to drive Stripe&#39;s onboarding programs. This is a high-impact role at the intersection of growth strategy, product management, and cross-organizational program ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In this role, you will own one of the most strategically consequential programs in Growth, driving the direction, health, and outcomes of Stripe&#39;s onboarding experience end-to-end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will set the program strategy in partnership with Growth leadership, holding organizations accountable to the success of the program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-org decisions across DRIs in Growth, Dashboard, Docs, Marketing, and product teams actively resolving the hard, ambiguous integration and ownership questions that fall between team boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and shape product and engineering roadmaps bringing a program-level perspective to team planning cycles, and advocating for cross-cutting investments that no single team will prioritize on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program management experience with demonstrated success in driving complex cross organizational programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and ability to understand enterprise customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to communicate with precision and credibility across engineering, product, and executive audiences, translating complex technical trade-offs into strategic decisions, and driving alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead and align cross-functional teams — driving decisions, resolving conflict, and building consensus across organizations with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successful program delivery in complex technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in product management or product operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

